{:edb/db-before-t 805 :edb/db-after-t 806 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534118 50 #inst "2026-10-11T16:52:27.626Z" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186133803 1038 #edb/ref 17592186410810 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186133803 1038 #edb/ref 17592186410811 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186133906 1038 #edb/ref 17592186410808 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186133906 1038 #edb/ref 17592186410809 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186134112 1068 #edb/ref 17592186130828 13194139534118 17592186045417 false] [17592186134112 1068 #edb/ref 17592186410805 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186134112 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186134112 1071 "$$\nx=\\,{Q}^{T}\\,\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186134112 1071 "$x = AQ^{T}A$\n\nLet $A = QR$ be a QR decomposition of an $m \\cdot n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax = b$. From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" 13194139534118 17592186045417 false] [17592186134112 1074 "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}\\,\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are ${R}^{-1}$ and $b.$" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410812 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410813 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410814 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410815 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1043 #edb/ref 17592186410816 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1045 "Finding a Least-Squares Solution Using QR Factorization" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1046 #edb/ref 17592186410813 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046673 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049845 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410777 1053 #uuid "9b29a2c1-0e8f-51a5-8bb4-88c6d8d5a680" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410778 1080 "$R$ and ${b}^{T}$" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410778 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410778 1083 #uuid "05f55e0b-2bfd-5324-bb60-ef44a8ce8695" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410779 1080 "{R}^{T}" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410779 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410779 1083 #uuid "09435933-4c28-52dd-8678-41dcf0848333" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410780 1080 "${R}^{-1}$ and $b$" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410780 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410780 1083 #uuid "0acc060c-c80f-5318-9ceb-31102a3b5205" 13194139534118 17592186045417 true] [17592186410781 1080 "